A||N||1||DaveL||Marker Light Retainers||||5||
Z||000000||DaveL||04-09-2001||03:52 PM||||I've noticed that a few of my side marker lights have one screw that doesn't tighten up. There seems to be something missing here, are there some sort of retainers that these screw into?<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroJoe||04-09-2001||10:09 PM||||Yes there are some retainers in there. They are called U-Nuts.  They are basically a little clip that you snap onto the fender peice under the marker light, and then the screw screws into it.  Take off your marker light and look for one either missing or in the wrong spot, causing the screw to basically try to tighten up it air.  You can get replacements at most hardware or autoparts stores.<P>Take one off that you know works and bring it with you to get the right size.  Also, there are some u-nuts that are made for use with machine screws (threads), so make sure you get some that are to be used with sheet metal screws (marker light screws), you'll be able to see the difference easily.<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
